		{
			dependencies: [
				"6F32A8739D8E792A"
				"4A96659253CCFACF"
			]
			description: [
				"This quest teaches you the basics about &bApplied Energistics 2&r autocrafting. If you are new to this mod, it is highly recommended that you watch a video or &3&lread the built-in guide&r&r. Just remember that channels are disabled by default in this pack."
				""
				"By now, you should have &6ME Pattern Providers, &6Molecular Assemblers, Crafting Units, Patterns&r and a &6Pattern Encoding Terminal&r. "
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"First, for all crafts, you'll need a &eCrafting CPU&r. These are structures that must be in a solid rectangular prism composed of:"
				""
				"&6* Crafting Storages&r, which determine how big a craft can be. For now, &64k Crafting Storages&r should be enough. You must have at least one per CPU."
				""
				"&6* Co-Processing Units&r, which allow the system to start multiple crafting steps at once. While these are optional, they greatly speed up crafting once your machines are fast enough to keep up."
				""
				"&6* Crafting Monitors&r, used to see what is crafting. Not needed, and you can right-click on the CPU to find out what is crafting anyways, so this is pretty much just decoration."
				""
				"&6* Crafting Units&r, which aren't needed at all, and are just used to fill holes if you have a lack of materials."
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"Second, you'll need the place for the autocrafting. For Crafting Table recipes, you'll need &6Molecular Assemblers&r. &6Pattern Providers&r are placed next to them. Autocrafting with &bGregTech&r is explained later, in the quest following this one."
				""
				"Finally, you'll need a &6Pattern&r. In order to make this, put empty &6Patterns&r in the &6Pattern Encoding Terminal&r, and find the recipe in &bEMI&r, while still in the &6Pattern Encoding Terminal&r. Then, click '+' in &bEMI&r, and press the arrow to encode the recipe. This goes in the &6Pattern Provider&r that you set up in the last step. You can use &6Pattern Access Terminals&r to access &6Pattern Providers'&r pattern slots.\n&2You can also manually encode patterns by adding items to individual slots in the Encoding Terminal, though there are not many use cases for this.&r"
				""
				"Eventually, you'll need a lot of &6Patterns&r, lots of CPUs, and ones with more storage, and lots of &6&6&6Pattern Providers&r&r&r. If you run out of pattern slots in a &6Pattern Provider&r, you can add more &6Pattern Providers&r, or use &6Extended Pattern Providers&r, which have 36 slots each."
			]
			icon: "ae2:crafting_monitor"
			id: "0EF85170074E70B3"
			shape: "hexagon"
			size: 1.5d
			tasks: [{
				id: "584BEA5276908468"
				title: "Setting up Autocrafting"
				type: "checkmark"
			}]
			x: 2.0d
			y: 6.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: [
				"41B4EA53D6D7AE37"
