		{
			dependencies: ["6F32A8739D8E792A"]
			description: [
				"The &6Molecular Assembler&r is the most flexible way to autocraft recipes that would otherwise be done in the &3Crafting Table&r, &3Stonecutter&r, or &3Smithing Table&r."
				""
				"Place one next to a &6Pattern Provider&r with a compatible &6Pattern&r and it will perform those recipe types when requested, no further configuration required."
				""
				"It can also craft recipes passively if supplied with a compatible &6Pattern&r and &aAE&r power."
			]
			id: "3C3E015DFA8FDECE"
			shape: "hexagon"
			tasks: [{
				id: "1FE22A73493AA6D9"
				item: "ae2:molecular_assembler"
				type: "item"
			}]
			x: 3.75d
			y: 6.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: [
				"2A6E9E7C80754936"
				"4FF4697A8AF10731"
			]
			description: [
				"&6ME Pattern Buffers&r are unlocked after you obtain &6Europium&r. These blocks work quite similarly to &6Pattern Providers&r, with some notable differences. They are used in a multiblocks' structure as a bus/hatch. The items/fluids provided from patterns in the buffer are stored in an infinitely large internal storage. Each pattern has its own buffer, so no two patterns can mix ingredients. Additionally, catalyst items/fluids can be shared across all patterns in the buffer.\n&9Note that Pattern Buffers don't support blocking mode. While this isn't usually an issue, you might want to use regular &6Pattern Providers&9 if you need some form of blocking mode.&r"
				""
				"Later, after building and running a &3Research Station&r, you will be able to make &6ME Pattern Buffer Proxies&r. They can be linked to a parent ME Pattern Buffer by Shift + Right-Clicking on the Buffer with a &6Data Stick&r then Right-Clicking on the Proxy with it. This will make it so that the internal inventory of the Buffer is available to the Proxy, for use in another multiblock."
			]
			id: "436707C1C1A6A9DC"
			shape: "hexagon"
			tasks: [{
				id: "6533101146563E11"
				item: "gtceu:me_pattern_buffer"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "ME Pattern Buffers and Proxies"
			x: 7.75d
			y: -2.75d
		}
		{
			dependencies: [
				"7C0A37EEA3C63B16"
				"605062720747B482"
			]
			description: [
				"These blocks function similarly to &6ME Input Buses&r/&6Hatches&r. Rather than specifying an amount to keep, the bus/hatch will make all items/fluid of that type in the network accessible to the multiblock. This does not actually pull the items from the network, so they are still available for use everywhere else in on the network."
				""
				"If the 'automatic pulling' mode is enabled, the first 16 items/fluid on the network will be made available to the multiblock."
			]
			id: "4FF4697A8AF10731"
			shape: "hexagon"
			tasks: [
				{
					id: "6A607A8AF587BBE5"
					item: "gtceu:me_stocking_input_bus"
					type: "item"
				}
				{
					id: "72872891101D9254"
					item: "gtceu:me_stocking_input_hatch"
					type: "item"
				}
			]
			title: "ME Stocking Buses"
			x: 6.5d
			y: -2.75d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["7E59E0E33962D787"]
			description: [
				"&6Level Emitters&r emit a redstone signal if there is above/below a certain amount of a selected item in the network that the Emitter is attached to. Not selecting an item will make the Emitter read the total amount of any item in the network"
				""
				"These are very useful for turning on/off machines using &6Machine Controllers&r."
			]
			id: "6D2CFBF365E052D5"
			shape: "hexagon"
			tasks: [{
				id: "39E7EB00A6D4EB9E"
				item: "ae2:level_emitter"
				type: "item"
			}]
			x: 4.0d
			y: -2.75d
		}
		{
			dependencies: [
				"521977C7165229F1"
				"6E27B9938B280291"
				"6DAB13A7BDECE94E"
			]
			description: [
				"&6ME Requesters&r allow you to select items that will be automatically requested when their stock drops below a specified level. They also allow you to set how large a batch will be requested."
				""
				"&6ME Requester Terminals&r allows you to see and edit all Requesters on the network."
			]
			id: "24312649E417990B"
			shape: "hexagon"
			tasks: [{
				id: "73884B63227783BD"
				item: "merequester:requester"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "ME Requesters"
			x: 0.75d
			y: 7.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["6D03BB4A6A4BBA27"]
			description: ["Fluix can be made via in-world crafting, by dropping &6Redstone&r, &6Nether Quartz&r, and a &6Charged Certus Quartz Crystal&r in the same block of &9Water&r. Alternatively, there is a recipe that uses power in a &3Mixer&r."]
			id: "491180694DA10086"
			shape: "hexagon"
			tasks: [{
				id: "68188F6A8A7F508F"
				item: "ae2:fluix_crystal"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "Fluix Crystals"
			x: 2.0d
			y: -6.25d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["491180694DA10086"]
			description: [
				"Fluix is initially made via in-world crafting, by dropping &6Redstone&r, &6Nether Quartz&r, and a &6Charged Certus Quartz Crystal&r in the same block of &9Water&r. You'll see some sparks then the items will merge into a &6Fluix Crystal&r. Be sure to turn off any nearby item magnets/collectors or they might interrupt this crafting process."
				""
				"The &3Energy Acceptor&r converts GT power into AE power that Applied Energistics uses, in a 1 EU to 2 AE ratio. This power will be transmitted through adjacent full-block ME Network devices, as well as along all connected &6ME Cables&r and &6Quartz Fibers&r."
				""
				"Quartz Fibers are &emicroparts&r you can put between an ME Cable and any ME Network block or another ME Cable. This will allow transmission of AE power but not data, which is useful for having data-isolated ME Networks all sharing the same power source."
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"Applied Energistics 2 can be complicated for a new player, so it is recommended to either &l&3use the in-game guide&r &e(Press G while hovering over a compatible item)&r or a video as a supplement to this chapter if need be. "
				""
				"[\"\",{\"text\":\"You can also look at \"},{\"color\":\"blue\",\"underlined\":true,\"text\":\"Pansmith's guide to Applied Energistics 2\",\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"copy_to_clipboard\",\"value\":\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=u0ouTWgdcXk\"},\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_text\",\"contents\":{\"text\":\"Click to copy to clipboard!\"}}},{\"text\":\". While written for the 1.12 version of AE2, most of the information is the exact same between the versions.\"}]"
			]
			icon: "ae2:energy_acceptor"
			id: "4174A6C6403DD245"
			rewards: [
				{
					id: "67642A41B1F7F4E8"
					item: "kubejs:moni_nickel"
					type: "item"
				}
				{
					id: "2EAC8635F1C7A8DB"
					item: "ae2:guide"
					type: "item"
				}
			]
			shape: "hexagon"
			size: 1.5d
			tasks: [{
				id: "652709622C84E4CC"
				item: "ae2:energy_acceptor"
				type: "item"
			}]
			x: 2.0d
			y: -4.25d
		}
